From b5d08853dbf4e24894d56942c07a5a743438e824 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:01:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Deus Ex AI: NPCs see -- IsValidEnemy, AICanSee and
 AIVisibility

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

A Deus Ex NPC finds its enemies in ScriptedPawn.CheckEnemyPresence: it cycles
through the pawns, keeps those IsValidEnemy accepts and asks AICanSee how
well it sees each; what it sees enough of, it attacks. None of it worked, so
no NPC ever noticed the player, or anyone:

- IsValidEnemy (native 2105) took only ScriptedPawns, never the player; it
  tested this pawn's bBlockSight and bDeleteMe where the original tests the
  other's bDetectable and bDeleteMe, and KillCount where it tests Health;
  and an omitted bCheckAlliance read as false, which returned false, where
  the original's exec function defaults it to true.
- AICanSee (native 705) and AIVisibility (701) were stubs returning 0.

Each is now the original's logic, read from DeusEx.dll and Engine.dll and
checked field by field against the Actor and Pawn layouts in the game's own
script source. AICanSee: from the eyes, the other's apparent size (nothing
under MinAngularSize), how much of it is inside a view AIHorizontalFov wide
and AspectRatio times narrower up and down (turned by AIAddViewRotation; at
least 0.75 up and down within 150 units), how lit it is (AIVisibility), less
VisibilityThreshold; then a line past the world and past any actor that
blocks sight and is not hidden: to its middle, or with bCheckCylinder to a
player's eyes, top and bottom, and another pawn's top, bottom and sides.
The defaults are the exec function's (1.0, true, true, false, true).
AIVisibility: the light on the actor, found again after a quarter second
and eased between findings -- half of each light reaching it by brightness,
whiteness and distance inside its radius, a static light only with no wall
or mover between, and twice the zone's ambient light -- and up to half as
much again at 30 to 200 units a second.

Supporting it:
- CollisionSystem::SightBlocked, the original's MultiLineCheck with
  NF_NotVisBlocking as a yes or no: the cells along the ray, as patch 0026
  walks them for TraceAnyHit (now through TraceTester::VisitActorsOnRay),
  every actor there asked, then the world's visibility-blocking surfaces,
  with no margin past the end. TraceActor traced no actor cylinders with
  visibilityOnly; no caller asked for both before this.
- AIVisibility takes the lights from the light system's tree, built each
  frame from the same test the original's scan of every actor makes: the
  few whose reach may take in the location, not a cache miss per actor
  (0.55 ms of the Smart Pro's tick as a walk of the whole light list). On
  Liberty Island it gave the whole list's answer over 2,000 calls.
- Actor.bDetectable, a Deus Ex property.

Checked on Liberty Island on the desktop: NPCs of hostile alliances now
check each other with AICanSee; with the player moved in front of an NSF
terrorist, it saw the player (visibility ~0.05 at night, rising as it
closed in), made the player its enemy ~3.5 s later -- the build-up
CheckCycle gives a faint sighting -- and two more joined in shooting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
